+# Aegis AI Platform — Production Infrastructure Provisioning Runbook
+
+This runbook collects the scripts, manifests and steps needed to provision production infrastructure for:
+- KMS keys & GitHub Actions OIDC/IAM role mapping
+- Rekor with TLS/Ingress
+- ExternalSecrets operator + SecretStore
+- Presidio (Analyzer + Anonymizer)
+- HA Postgres (Bitnami PostgreSQL HA) and object store (MinIO or S3)
+- GPU node pools, autoscaling and batching/caching for detectors
+- Admission validation: signature / Rekor checks webhook + Gatekeeper
+- A2A approver: hardened service with audit trail and signing via KMS
+- PREEMPT_RT node image build helper
+- Compliance: encrypted retention of originals, Presidio verification
+
+This file references scripts and manifests included in this patch. Follow the numbered steps in order.
+
+Prerequisites
+- kubectl, helm, aws/gcloud/az CLIs (as appropriate), cert-manager installed (for TLS), GitHub repo admin.
+- A container registry to push detector and approver images.
+- Access to cloud account to create KMS keys and node pools.
+
+1) Create KMS keys and minimal privilege signing role (AWS example)
+- Create KMS key (asymmetric or symmetric): see scripts/aws_create_kms_key.sh
+- Create OIDC IAM role for GitHub Actions: scripts/setup_aws_oidc_kms.sh <org> <repo> <kms-key-arn> <role-name>
+- Add role ARN and COSIGN_KMS_URI to GitHub Secrets (COSIGN_KMS_URI example: aws-kms://arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123:alias/aegis-sign)
+- Review iam/kms_sign_policy.json for minimal actions (kms:Sign, kms:DescribeKey, kms:GetPublicKey)
+
+2) Deploy Rekor with TLS (cert-manager)
+- Install Rekor via Helm or apply k8s/rekor/deployment.yaml
+- Apply k8s/rekor/ingress-tls.yaml (ensure DNS rekor.example.com points to ingress)
+- Set REKOR_SERVER in GitHub Secrets to https://rekor.example.com
+
+3) Install ExternalSecrets operator and SecretStore
+- Run k8s/external-secrets/install_external_secrets.sh
+- Apply the SecretStore manifest that matches your cloud (external-secrets/secretstore-*.yaml)
+- Create ExternalSecret for MCP DB: external-secrets/externalsecret-mcp-postgres.yaml
+
+4) Provision HA Postgres and object store
+- Use Bitnami PostgreSQL HA chart:
+  helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami
+  helm install mcp-postgres bitnami/postgresql-ha -f helm/postgres/values.yaml
+- Or use your managed cloud Postgres with high-availability and point ExternalSecret to it.
+- For object store, deploy MinIO (k8s/minio/minio-deploy.yaml) or use S3/GCS/Azure Blob.
+
+5) Deploy Presidio (PII)
+- Apply k8s/presidio/presidio-deploy.yaml
+- Validate PRESIDIO_ANALYZER endpoint reachable by the PII adapter service
+- Configure anonymizer policies appropriately; run tests under tests/adversarial/pii_samples.txt
+
+6) Build & deploy detector images, batching proxies, and autoscaling
+- Build detector images (moderation/verifier/batcher) and push to registry.
+- Deploy charts (helm/detectors) or apply k8s/moderation/* and k8s/verifier/* manifests.
+- Ensure node pool with GPU labels exists and nodeSelector in manifests is correct (k8s/gpu/node-labels.yaml is example).
+- Install Cluster Autoscaler (cloud-specific) and configure HPA manifests (k8s/moderation/moderation-hpa.yaml, k8s/verifier/verifier-hpa.yaml).
+
+7) Gatekeeper & Admission checks
+- Install Gatekeeper: k8s/gatekeeper/install_gatekeeper.sh
+- Apply Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplate/Constraint (k8s/gatekeeper/* from repo)
+- Deploy validating admission webhook for signature+Rekor checks:
+  - Deploy service: k8s/admission/webhook-deploy.yaml
+  - Apply ValidatingWebhookConfiguration: k8s/admission/webhook-config.yaml
+- Webhook service will enforce that workloads have annotation `mcp.provenance/signed=true` and optional `mcp.provenance/rekor_digest=<base64>` and will verify Rekor if REKOR_SERVER is configured.
+
+8) Harden A2A approver
+- Deploy A2A approver service (services/a2a/approver_service.py) which:
+  - Requires JWT/OAuth token for approval requests
+  - Persists approvals and audit trail in Postgres
+  - Signs approval records using KMS (AWS example implemented)
+- Configure approver's DB credentials via ExternalSecret and set APPROVER_JWT_SECRET (or connect to OIDC provider)
+
+9) PREEMPT_RT & HIL
+- Use scripts/preempt/build_preempt_rt_image.sh as a starting point to build node images with PREEMPT_RT kernel (requires operator input and HW).
+- Provision a test cluster or node pool with the built image, label nodes for runtime scheduling.
+- Run HIL jobs and produce signed evidence packs stored in MCP.
+
+10) Provenance completeness & CI integration
+- Use .github/workflows/cosign_aws_oidc_sign.yml or .github/workflows/cosign_kms_rekor_all.yml (multi-provider) to sign artifacts with KMS and upload to Rekor.
+- After signing, run scripts/save_sig_to_s3.sh to store artifact and .sig together.
+- CI should also call scripts/test_rekor_upload.sh to assert Rekor entry exists; fail build if absent.
+
+11) Compliance & original retention
+- When redaction happens, original raw artifacts must be encrypted with KMS and stored in a restricted bucket.
+- Use scripts/encrypt_and_store_original.sh to encrypt with KMS and upload to S3; store pointer + access control in MCP and require A2A approval to retrieve.
+
+12) Testing & validation
+- Run load tests: scripts/load_test_detectors.py against detector endpoints and tune HPA.
+- Run adversarial tests: .github/workflows/adversarial_ci.yml triggers tests/run_adversarial.py which exercises NSFW/PII/verifier corpora.
+- Verify end-to-end signing and Rekor entries with scripts/test_rekor_upload.sh
+
+Notes & cautions
+- Many scripts assume AWS as example. For GCP / Azure / HashiCorp Vault, adapt KMS / IAM steps accordingly.
+- PREEMPT_RT image building is hardware-specific and requires kernel build expertise.
+- This runbook is intended to be executed by platform operators with cloud admin privileges.
+
